  "executive_briefing": "As of late 2026, the global corporate tax landscape has consolidated around the OECD Pillar Two 15% effective minimum tax, permanently halting the historic race to the bottom in statutory corporate tax rates. Jurisdictions, particularly within the ASEAN region, are proactively recalibrating their fiscal incentives away from traditional tax holidays toward compliant refundable tax credits. Concurrently, real-time digital tax administration has accelerated through Peppol-based e-invoicing mandates, such as Singapore's InvoiceNow initiative. Meanwhile, international trade continues to face severe volatility driven by aggressive, protectionist tariff cycles and unilateral customs policies.",
